  "limitations": [
    "Performance A/B used isolated source snapshots, not the final portable EXE. Its baseline is identified by commit and the performance-only snapshot by its complete file inventory.",
    "The A/B snapshots kept the old startup configuration/package metadata/main adapter and deliberately excluded the separate caster projectile lifetime startup change. Final portable behavior is tested separately.",
    "Measurements cover short approximately three-second starting phases with 500 soldiers per side, not sustained dense combat or a soak test. No RNG seed or external desktop-load control was used.",
    "Requested 8x would require 240 simulation steps/second; measured 129.25 in the source A/B overview is only about 4.31x. Neither 8x/20x speed nor 240 FPS is guaranteed.",
    "Render CPU/presentation counters are not physical display refresh or GPU completion. The CPU-only benchmark excludes renderer, audio, Electron and GUI and includes cases that regress.",
    "The reported prior 32 GB memory peak was not reproduced or causally diagnosed. Process working-set sums may double-count shared pages, and JS heap excludes GPU/native allocations.",
    "All 28 published asset sizes and SHA-256 digests match local files via GitHub API; a full remote redownload was not performed. The public version tag points to the verified runtime commit."
